<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Federal War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1859">1859</a>–<a href="/years/1863">1863</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Long War (Venezuela), Five Years' War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Federal War was a civil war in Venezuela from 1859 to 1863 between the Conservatives and the Liberals, who demanded a federal system. Federalist leaders such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ezequiel-zamora">Ezequiel Zamora</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-crisostomo-falcon">Juan Crisóstomo Falcón</a> fought a largely <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war in which many thousands died. It ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-coche">Treaty of Coche</a> in 1863 and a federal constitution in 1864.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/federal-war.jpg" alt="Federal War" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Combate_de_Maiquetia,_el_2_de_septiembre_de_1859.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
